 Ashcroft. <year>2007</year>. Identification of the PIP<sub>2</sub>-binding site on Kir6.2 by molecular modelling and functional analysis. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>26</volume>:<fpage>3749</fpage>&#x02013;3759.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17673911</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Hardie, R.C. <year>2007</year>. TRP channels and lipids: from Drosophila to mammalian physiology. <source>J. Physiol.</source> <volume>578</volume>:<fpage>9</fpage>&#x02013;24.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16990401</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Harlan, J.E., P.J. Hajduk, H.S. Yoon, and S.W. Fesik. <year>1994</year>. Pleckstrin homology domains bind to phosphatidylinositol-4,5-bisphosphate. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>371</volume>:<fpage>168</fpage>&#x02013;170.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8072546</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Ho, I.H., and R.D. Murrell-Lagnado. <year>1999</year>. Molecular mechanism for sodium-dependent activation of G protein-gated K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channels. <source>J. Physiol.</source> <volume>520</volume>(Pt 3):<fpage>645</fpage>&#x02013;651.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10545132</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Howard, R.J., K.A. Clark, J.M. Holton, and D.L. Minor Jr. <year>2007</year>. Structural insight into KCNQ (Kv7) channel assembly and channelopathy. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>53</volume>:<fpage>663</fpage>&#x02013;675.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17329207</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Jentsch, T.J. <year>2000</year>. Neuronal KCNQ potassium channels: physiology and role in disease. <source>Nat. Rev. Neurosci.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>21</fpage>&#x02013;30.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11252765</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Lemmon, M.A. <year>2003</year>. Phosphoinositide recognition dom